{
  "_comment": [
    "US-124 / ADR 0091 corpus oracle, pinned 2026-09-04 from the app's own parser",
    "(window.__braAutoModeDebug.dxf.parse on dxf.decodeBytes(<file bytes>)).",
    "`patterns` = pieces the parser must return; for every INSERT-based file it equals",
    "the top-level INSERT count now that duplicate block names resolve k-th INSERT ->",
    "k-th BLOCK and GBK names decode correctly. `orphans` must be 0 everywhere.",
    "`lines` = kept segments after Phase 3 dedupe (exact duplicates always dropped,",
    "ASTM quality-validation twins dropped by default); `droppedExact`/`droppedQv` pin",
    "what dedupe removed. Legacy-only files keep every line (dedupe never touches them).",
    "Files with no closed ASTM layer-1 chain at all (3380, 2927) are pinned to their",
    "pre-ADR-0091 legacy count. SN1252 (27/28 instances), DM7549 (2/25) and MHB001",
    "(4/45) still have instances whose layer-1 chains do not close and fall back per",
    "instance; their totals equal the INSERT count anyway. A change to any row is a",
    "regression unless a follow-up re-pins it deliberately with the reason recorded.",
    "Excluded on purpose: 2892XL-new.dxf (24 legacy pieces, ~30 s parse — too slow",
    "for CI), the three 16-36 MB 齐码 files, and 2756.dxf / 2938常规L.dxf (no",
    "supported entities; unchanged 'empty' rejection)."
  ],
